  "kind": "tangent_plane",
  "title": "Tangent plane to a sphere",
  "prompt": "Find an equation of the tangent plane to the sphere $x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 14$ at $(1, 2, 3)$.",
  "answer_format": "An equation in x, y and z.",
  "difficulty": 2,
  "tags": [
    "tangent plane",
    "level surfaces"
  ],
  "data": {
    "surface": "x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 14",
    "at": [
      "1",
      "2",
      "3"
    ]
  },
  "answer": "x + 2y + 3z = 14",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "Write the sphere as F(x, y, z) = 14. The gradient ∇F at the point is a normal vector to the plane."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "$F = x^2 + y^2 + z^2$, $\\nabla F = \\langle 2x, 2y, 2z\\rangle$, so $\\nabla F(1,2,3) = \\langle 2, 4, 6\\rangle$.",
    "$2(x - 1) + 4(y - 2) + 6(z - 3) = 0$, which simplifies to $x + 2y + 3z = 14$."
  ],
  "reference": {
    "book": "openstax-calc3",
    "section": "4.6 Directional Derivatives and the Gradient",
    "note": "Original problem; see tangent planes to level surfaces."
  },
  "review": {
    "status": "draft"
  },
  "examples": [
    {
      "name": "normal from the gradient",
      "submission": {
        "steps": [
          {
            "kind": "expr",
            "content": "F_x = 2x"
          },
